\u2019s happening now, not when we have so much to do. My friends notice my distress and stop talking, their faces an anxious mix of worry and determination.\n\nI look over at Yuri, and in her eyes, I see fear and confusion. She\u2019s been there for me through so much, and now it\u2019s my turn to lean on her. \"Natsuki, are you okay? Are those contractions?\" she asks, her voice barely above a whisper.\n\nI take a deep breath, trying to hold back the tears. \"I-I think so, but they seem too early\u2026 I was only 36 weeks, and I was supposed to give birth at 40. Yuri, I don\u2019t know what to do. We have to finish this mission first...\"\n\nYuri's eyes fill with tears, and she takes my hand. \"We will, Natsuki. First, you have to focus on yourself and our baby. We\u2019ll get MC after you\u2019re both safe.\"\n\nMy heart is racing, but I know she\u2019s right. I fight back the panic and try to stay strong for us both. \"Okay, let\u2019s move to the hospital. We can take care of Hope and still stop MC.\"\n\nThe journey is a blur as we rush to the hospital, my friends surrounding me, offering their support. In the sterile, white-walled room, I lie down on the bed, the pain searing through me. My friends watch anxiously as I begin to struggle to bring Hope into the world.\n\nIt\u2019s an endless cycle of contractions, each one more intense than the last. Pain and relief, pain and relief, as I push as hard as I can. Lunagaron and Yuri take turns holding my hand, whispering words of encouragement, but the hours feel like an eternity. My vision blurs, and I can\u2019t tell where the walls end"}, {"key": [51, 2, "iso"], "traj": 0, "log_surv_q": -7.060202239682714e-10, "log_surv_s": -1.2991486346408347e-09, "gen_len": 273, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [51, 2, "iso"], "traj": 1, "log_surv_q": -6.344990936981093e-09, "log_surv_s": -9.835045207775075e-09, "gen_len": 342, "bail_leak": false}, {"key": [51, 2, "iso"], "traj": 2, "log_surv_q": -1.8179552000624787e-09, "log_surv